course: dictionary
lesson: 13977
title: Words for places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal, so you hear them in school reports, maps and official letters more than in chatting with friends. Locality is one of these. Its everyday cousin is area or neighbourhood. «Our school is in a quiet locality with parks and shops.» The clues are parks and shops, so a locality is a place you could walk around and get to know.
explain: Locality can also mean an exact spot. «The scientist wrote down the locality of every fossil she found.» Here the sentence is about where something was found, not about a whole neighbourhood. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about a wide area, or one exact place? The words around the word tell you which.
explain: Look for the phrase «in the locality», which means in the area around a place. «Please tell the police if you see anything strange in the locality.» It means close by, in the places near where you are. Try swapping in area: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Locality» is a noun, so you can say «a locality» or «localities».
fact: «Locality» means an area or neighbourhood, the place around a particular point.
fact: In science, «locality» can mean the exact place where something was found, such as a rock, a plant or a fossil.
fact: Everyday talk usually says «area» or «neighbourhood» instead of «locality».
fact: Useful phrases include «in the locality» and «the immediate locality», which means the area right around a place.
exercise: «The school is in a quiet locality with parks and shops.» What does locality mean here? | A kind of lesson | A type of rock | A very loud noise | *An area or neighbourhood
exercise: In a science report: «The fossil was found at a locality near the river.» What does locality mean in this sentence? | *The exact place where it was found | A group of children on a trip | A kind of rain | A map of the night sky
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as locality? | fossil | sample | *area | castle
test: «Mum says the immediate locality is safe to walk in.» What does the immediate locality mean? | A long journey by train | A school rule about bags | *The area right around us | The inside of a house
test: In geography, you might be asked about «your locality». What is it asking about? | A list of your favourite books | The weather forecast for next week | The name of a famous castle | *Your local area, with its shops, parks and roads
exam: A scientist writes, «The sample came from a rocky locality.» Why does she use the word locality? | Because locality is a shorter word for area | *Because it is the exact place where the sample was found | Because she is talking about her favourite food | Because locality is a kind of rock
